{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 13, :comments ["<b>HaShem your Elohim you shall fear, and Him you shall serve, and by His name you shall swear.</b> By way of the plain sense (peshat): when you have occasion to swear to fulfill and to do some matter that you wish, you shall not swear by the name of other elohim, but only by the name of the Blessed One alone; and this is 'and by His name you shall swear.' And this is not a positive commandment to swear." "<b>And our Rabbis, of blessed memory,</b> interpreted in the Sifre: 'and by His name you shall swear' — if you possess all these traits, fearing sin and serving your Creator, then 'by His name you shall swear'; for out of the fact that you fear Him, you will be careful with an oath. And it is known that everyone who is a lover is a fearer, while there are some who are fearers and not lovers. If so, then fear is included within love. And this is what it says here: 'HaShem your Elohim you shall fear,' after it mentioned 'and you shall love HaShem your Elohim' — for first He admonished concerning the trait of love and afterward He admonished concerning fear, because love includes everything, as has been explained many times. And in the section והיה עקב (Deuteronomy 10) He added 'and in Him you shall cling,' because there He mentioned above only 'in your fathers He delighted' (באבותיך חשק); therefore He says: since the Blessed One has distinguished your matter above all other nations in the matter of delight and clinging, it is fitting for you also that you cling to Him — for if the Creator desires the clinging of the created being, how much more so is the created being obligated to desire clinging to his Creator."], :book :deuteronomy, :voice :rabbeinu-bahya, :lang :en, :chapter 6, :notes {1 "רז״ל resolved as רבותינו זכרונם לברכה based on the reference to the Sifre; א״כ resolved as אם כן; אח״כ resolved as אחר כך."}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T13:46:11.477645073Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}